# Manual Testing - Complete Notes & Theory

## Executive Overview

Manual testing is the process of **manually exploring and testing software** without using automated test scripts. A QA tester executes test cases, observes results, and reports defects.

**Key Characteristics:**
- ✓ Human-driven testing
- ✓ Exploratory in nature
- ✓ Immediate feedback
- ✓ Visual/UX evaluation
- ✓ User perspective validation
- ✓ No automation framework needed

