### 1. **The 12 Principles of Manual Testing**

```
1. INDEPENDENCE
   ├─ Each test case stands alone
   ├─ No test depends on another
   └─ Can run in any order

2. CLARITY
   ├─ Clear test cases
   ├─ Unambiguous steps
   ├─ Obvious expected results
   └─ No guessing

3. COVERAGE
   ├─ Test happy path
   ├─ Test error cases
   ├─ Test edge cases
   └─ Test boundary values

4. REPRODUCIBILITY
   ├─ Same steps = same results
   ├─ Consistent environment
   ├─ Detailed documentation
   └─ Can be repeated reliably

5. EFFICIENCY
   ├─ Don't waste time
   ├─ Risk-based approach
   ├─ Prioritize tests
   └─ Use time wisely

6. COLLABORATION
   ├─ Talk to team
   ├─ Share findings
   ├─ Pair testing sessions
   └─ Learn from others

7. DOCUMENTATION
   ├─ Document everything
   ├─ Clear notes
   ├─ Screenshots when needed
   └─ Traceable results

8. DEFECT MINDSET
   ├─ Try to break it
   ├─ Think like user
   ├─ Test edge cases
   └─ Verify assumptions

9. COMMUNICATION
   ├─ Clear bug reports
   ├─ Timely reporting
   ├─ Follow up on fixes
   └─ Feedback loop

10. CONTINUOUS LEARNING
    ├─ Learn the application
    ├─ Understand business
    ├─ Improve skills
    └─ Share knowledge

11. PRECISION
    ├─ Follow steps exactly
    ├─ Don't skip actions
    ├─ Note exact behavior
