### 2. **What NOT to Do**

```
❌ ANTI-PATTERNS:

1. SKIPPING STEPS
   Wrong: "I already know what this does"
   Right: Follow every step, every time
   Why: One skip = one missed bug

2. ASSUMING BEHAVIOR
   Wrong: "It probably works like before"
   Right: Test explicitly
   Why: Changes can have side effects

3. COPY-PASTE BUGS
   Wrong: Use same data every time
   Right: Vary test data
   Why: Miss bugs in data validation

4. VAGUE BUG REPORTS
   Wrong: "It's broken" with no detail
   Right: Complete reproduction steps
   Why: Developer can't reproduce = can't fix

5. TESTING WITHOUT PLAN
   Wrong: "I'll just test random stuff"
   Right: Structured test cases
   Why: Random testing is inefficient

6. IGNORING EDGE CASES
   Wrong: "That's an edge case, skip it"
   Right: Test boundaries and edges
   Why: That's where most bugs hide

7. NOT COMMUNICATING
   Wrong: Find 10 bugs, report nothing
   Right: Report bugs immediately
   Why: Developer can't fix unknown bugs

8. POOR DOCUMENTATION
   Wrong: No notes on what was tested
   Right: Detailed test logs
   Why: Need proof of testing for compliance

9. INCONSISTENT ENVIRONMENT
   Wrong: Test on different machines each time
   Right: Consistent test environment
   Why: Different results = unreliable

10. RETESTING TOO LONG
    Wrong: Test same case 100 times
    Right: Move on after verification
    Why: Diminishing returns on time spent
```

