### 1. **Mutation Testing Concepts**

Understanding how small changes reveal test weaknesses.

```
Original Code:
if (age >= 18) {
    allowAccess = true;
}

Mutation 1: Change >= to >
if (age > 18) {
    allowAccess = true;
}

Test Case: age = 18, expected: true

Original: ✓ PASS (18 >= 18 = true)
Mutant:   ✗ FAIL (18 > 18 = false) ← Test catches mutation

Test Quality: GOOD (catches change)

---

Mutation 2: Change true to false
if (age >= 18) {
    allowAccess = false;  // Changed
}

Test Case: age = 20, expected: true

Original: ✓ PASS (allowAccess = true)
Mutant:   ✓ PASS (allowAccess = false) ← Test doesn't catch!

Test Quality: POOR (missed mutation)
Need Better Test:
- Test age = 20, expect true
- Test age = 16, expect false
```

