### Process 3: Defect Triage & Investigation

#### Theory Foundation
```
Triage Cycle:
New Bug → Verify → Classify → Assign → Fix → Verify → Close

Why This Matters:
- Filters out non-bugs early
- Ensures bugs reach right team
- Prioritizes critical issues
- Prevents duplicates
```

#### Step-by-Step Procedure

```
STEP 1: BUG RECEIVED

Initial State:
├─ Status: NEW
├─ Assigned: QA Lead for triage
├─ Priority: Not yet set
└─ Severity: Not yet set

Example Bug Report:
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ #456: Login not working     │
│ Reported: John Smith        │
│ Date: Dec 30, 14:32         │
│ Description: Can't login    │
└─────────────────────────────┘

Theory: First impression might be incomplete
- May lack details
- May be user error
- May be environment issue
- Need investigation


STEP 2: REPRODUCE (VERIFY)

Process:
├─ Follow exact steps provided
├─ Try with different data
├─ Try in different environment
├─ Try with different browser
└─ Try at different time

Reproduction Scenario:

Attempt 1: Exact reproduction
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Preconditions:                     │
│ - Browser: Chrome                  │
│ - OS: Windows 11                   │
│ - Build: v2.5.0-beta               │
│ - Environment: Staging             │
│ - Account: testuser@example.com    │
│                                    │
│ Steps:                             │
│ 1. Go to login page                │
│ 2. Enter email and password        │
│ 3. Click login                     │
│                                    │
│ Result: ✓ REPRODUCED              │
│ Error: "Login failed - try again"  │
│                                    │
│ Status: CONFIRMED BUG              │
└────────────────────────────────────┘

Theory: Confirming reproducibility is crucial
- If can't reproduce: Might be intermittent
- If easily reproduce: Likely critical bug
- Reproducibility = Bug quality


STEP 3: CLASSIFY

Decision Tree:

Is this reproducible?
├─ NO
│  ├─ Try different environment
│  ├─ Try different browser
│  ├─ Try different time
│  └─ If still no: Mark INTERMITTENT
│
└─ YES
   │
   ├─ Is this expected behavior?
   │  ├─ YES: Mark INVALID / WORKING AS DESIGNED
   │  │
   │  └─ NO: Proceed to severity assessment
   │
   ├─ How many users affected?
   │  ├─ ALL users: Severity HIGH/CRITICAL
   │  ├─ Some users: Severity MEDIUM
   │  └─ Edge case: Severity LOW
   │
   ├─ What's the impact?
   │  ├─ App crashes: CRITICAL
   │  ├─ Feature unusable: HIGH
   │  ├─ Feature impaired: MEDIUM
   │  └─ Minor issue: LOW
   │
   └─ When to fix?
      ├─ CRITICAL: Immediately
      ├─ HIGH: This sprint
      ├─ MEDIUM: Next sprint
      └─ LOW: Backlog

Classification Example:

Bug #456: Login not working

├─ Reproducibility: YES ✓ (easily)
│
├─ Expected Behavior: YES (should login) ✓
│
├─ Impact Assessment
│  ├─ Affected Users: All users trying to login
│  ├─ Current Time: Peak usage time (2 PM)
│  ├─ Feature Impact: Core functionality
│  └─ Business Impact: Revenue blocked
│
├─ Severity Classification
│  ├─ Symptoms: Cannot authenticate
│  ├─ Reproduction: 100% reproducible
│  ├─ User Impact: Complete feature loss
│  └─ SEVERITY: CRITICAL ⚠️
│
├─ Priority Classification
│  ├─ Timeline: Users can't use app NOW
│  ├─ Workaround: No workaround
│  ├─ Escalation: P0 incident
│  └─ PRIORITY: URGENT ⚠️
│
└─ Updated Classification:
   ├─ Status: CONFIRMED
   ├─ Severity: CRITICAL
   ├─ Priority: URGENT
   ├─ Assigned: Dev Lead (immediate)
   └─ Timeline: Fix within 1 hour


STEP 4: DETAILED INVESTIGATION

Process:
├─ Test different scenarios
├─ Isolate exact cause
├─ Check related features
├─ Investigate error logs
└─ Provide root cause analysis

Investigation Process:

Investigation Phase 1: Scope Isolation
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Q1: Is it ALL login attempts?│
│ A: No, works with Admin     │
│    account sometimes        │
│                             │
│ Q2: Specific email domain?  │
│ A: Affects all @example.com │
│    but not @internal.local  │
│                             │
│ Q3: Specific browser?       │
│ A: All browsers affected    │
│                             │
│ Q4: Time-dependent?         │
│ A: Started at 2:00 PM UTC   │
│                             │
│ Finding: Email domain       │
│          related issue      │
└─────────────────────────────┘

Investigation Phase 2: Root Cause

Hypothesis 1: Database connection issue?
- Action: Check server logs
- Result: Connections normal

Hypothesis 2: Email validation failing?
- Action: Test with different domains
- Result: @example.com fails, others work

Hypothesis 3: Recent code change?
- Action: Check deployment history
- Result: Email regex updated 1 hour ago

Finding: Recent regex change is too strict!

