#### Q9: What is Severity and Priority? Difference?

**Theory:**
Severity and Priority are **different dimensions** of bug classification:
- **Severity**: How bad is the bug? (impact)
- **Priority**: When to fix it? (urgency)

**They're Not the Same:**

```
SEVERITY (Impact on User)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CRITICAL                                │
│ - System crashes                        │
│ - Data loss                             │
│ - Core feature completely broken       │
│ - Can't proceed with testing           │
│ Example: Login broken for all users    │
│                                        │
│ HIGH                                    │
│ - Major functionality doesn't work     │
│ - Significant feature degradation      │
│ - Workaround very difficult            │
│ Example: Cart calculation wrong        │
│                                        │
│ MEDIUM                                  │
│ - Feature works but with issues        │
│ - Not ideal but usable                 │
│ - Workaround available                 │
│ Example: Payment processing slow       │
│                                        │
│ LOW                                     │
│ - Minor issue, rarely impacts user     │
│ - Just UI cosmetic                     │
│ - Workaround easy                      │
│ Example: Button text has typo          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘

PRIORITY (When to Fix)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ URGENT/P0                               │
│ - Fix immediately                      │
│ - Stop everything else                 │
│ - Deploy hot fix if needed             │
│ Timeline: Within 1 hour                │
│                                        │
│ HIGH/P1                                 │
│ - Fix this sprint                      │
│ - Before release                       │
│ Timeline: Days                         │
│                                        │
│ MEDIUM/P2                               │
│ - Fix next sprint                      │
│ - Can wait one cycle                   │
│ Timeline: 1-2 weeks                    │
│                                        │
│ LOW/P3                                  │
│ - Fix when time allows                 │
│ - Can defer indefinitely               │
│ Timeline: Backlog                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Real Examples (NOT Same):**

```
Example 1: Typo in Brand Name
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Issue: "Aple" instead of "Apple"│
│ Severity: LOW (cosmetic)       │
│ Priority: HIGH                 │
│ Why: Brand name wrong = major  │
│      reputational damage       │
│ Fix Timeline: Immediately     │
└────────────────────────────────┘

Example 2: Discount Not Applied
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Issue: 10% discount not working│
│ Severity: HIGH (wrong total)   │
│ Priority: LOW                  │
│ Why: Affects 1% of users      │
│      can refund manually      │
│ Fix Timeline: Next sprint     │
└────────────────────────────────┘

Example 3: System Crash
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Issue: App crashes on login    │
│ Severity: CRITICAL             │
│ Priority: URGENT (P0)          │
│ Why: No one can use it         │
│ Fix Timeline: Immediately     │
└────────────────────────────────┘

Example 4: Report Takes 5 Seconds
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Issue: Report slow, takes 5 sec│
│ Severity: MEDIUM (slow)        │
│ Priority: LOW                  │
│ Why: Hardly used feature       │
│      can optimize later        │
│ Fix Timeline: Backlog          │
└────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Classification Matrix:**

```
                    CRITICAL    HIGH        MEDIUM      LOW
┌──────────────────┬─────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
│ URGENT (P0)      │   ▓▓▓   │    ▓     │    ░     │    ░     │
