#### Q11: What is Test Double? Types: Stub, Mock, Fake, Spy?

**Theory:**
Test Doubles are **replacement objects** that mimic real objects in tests. They simulate external dependencies so you can test in isolation.

**Why Needed:**

```
Real Scenario: Testing without test doubles

Testing function: processPayment()

Function needs:
├─ Payment gateway (external, slow, costs money!)
├─ Email service (external, may be down)
├─ Database (may not have test data)
└─ Third-party API (rate limited)

Problems:
✗ Tests are slow (calls real services)
✗ Tests cost money (real transactions)
✗ Tests flaky (depends on external services)
✗ Tests can't test failure scenarios
✗ Tests run independently

Solution:
→ Replace with Test Doubles!
→ Tests fast, reliable, isolated
```

**Types of Test Doubles:**

```
1. STUB - Returns predefined values
   ├─ Purpose: Provide fixed responses
   ├─ Behavior: Only returns data
   ├─ Use: When you need specific return value
   │
   ├─ Example:
   │  Real: database.getUser(123)
   │         → Queries actual database
   │  
   │  Stub: database.getUser(123)
   │        → Always returns {id:123, name:"John"}
   │
   └─ Code:
      class StubPaymentGateway extends PaymentGateway {
          @Override
          public PaymentResult charge(amount) {
              return new PaymentResult(true, "success");
          }
      }


2. MOCK - Verifies correct calls made
   ├─ Purpose: Verify interactions
   ├─ Behavior: Records calls, verifies expectations
   ├─ Use: Test that right methods called correctly
   │
   ├─ Example:
   │  Mock tracks: Was sendEmail() called?
   │               Was it called with right email?
   │               Was it called exactly once?
   │
   └─ Code:
      MockEmailService emailService = new MockEmailService();
      
      // Test code calls this
      user.resetPassword();
      
      // Verify email was sent correctly
      emailService.verify()
          .sendEmail(called_once)
          .with("reset@example.com")
          .with(contains("reset link"));


3. FAKE - Simplified working implementation
   ├─ Purpose: Working alternative
   ├─ Behavior: Actual logic but simplified
   ├─ Use: When you need real behavior but simple
   │
   ├─ Example:
   │  Real: Connects to actual database
   │  Fake: In-memory data structure
   │
   │        Real: Takes 100ms per query
   │        Fake: Takes 1ms per query
   │
   └─ Code:
      class FakeUserDatabase implements UserDatabase {
          private Map<Integer, User> users = new HashMap<>();
          
          @Override
          public User findById(int id) {
              return users.get(id);  // In-memory
          }
      }


4. SPY - Records calls to real object
   ├─ Purpose: Verify real object was called correctly
   ├─ Behavior: Wraps real object, records calls
   ├─ Use: Partially mock real object
   │
   ├─ Example:
   │  Real object still works normally
   │  But spy records: "emailService.sendEmail() called"
   │
   └─ Code:
      RealEmailService realService = new RealEmailService();
      SpyEmailService spy = spy(realService);
      
      // Code uses spy (which uses real service underneath)
      user.resetPassword();
      
      // Verify was called
      verify(spy).sendEmail(any());
```

**Usage Scenario:**

```
Testing: Order.completeCheckout()

Requirements:
├─ Process payment (external service)
├─ Send confirmation email (external service)
├─ Update inventory (external service)
└─ Save to database (external service)

Without Test Doubles (PROBLEMS):
─────────────────────────────────
@Test
void testCheckout() {
    Order order = new Order();
    order.completeCheckout();
    
    // Wait: This calls REAL payment gateway
    // Wait: This sends REAL email
    // Wait: This calls REAL inventory service
    // Wait: This uses REAL database
    
    // Result: Test takes 30 seconds, costs $$$, may fail!
}


With Test Doubles (CLEAN):
──────────────────────────
@Test
void testCheckout() {
    // Setup test doubles
    PaymentGateway paymentStub = new StubPaymentGateway();
    EmailService emailMock = new MockEmailService();
    InventoryService inventoryFake = new FakeInventoryService();
    Database dbFake = new FakeDatabase();
    
    Order order = new Order(paymentStub, emailMock, 
                            inventoryFake, dbFake);
    
    // Execute
    order.completeCheckout();
    
    // Verify interactions
    assertEquals(PAID, order.getStatus());
    emailMock.verify().sendEmail(contains("confirmation"));
    
    // Result: Test in 100ms, no money spent, always reliable!
}
```

