#### Q15: What is Pairwise Testing?

**Theory:**
Pairwise (or All-Pairs) testing creates test cases where **every pair of parameters** is tested at least once.

**Why:**

```
Without Pairwise:
─────────────────
Suppose we have 5 parameters with 5 values each:
5^5 = 3,125 test cases!
Time: Impossible to execute all

With Pairwise:
──────────────
Instead of 3,125 combinations
We test every PAIR of parameters once
Result: ~20-30 test cases
Time: Practical and fast
```

**Example:**

```
Testing: Loan Application Form

Parameters:
├─ Age: [18, 25, 35, 50, 65]
├─ Income: [Low, Medium, High]
├─ Credit: [Poor, Fair, Good]
├─ Employment: [Employed, Self-Employed, Retired]
└─ Assets: [None, Some, Substantial]

Total Combinations: 5 × 3 × 3 × 3 × 2 = 270

With Pairwise Testing:
We ensure every pair is tested at least once

Example Pairs to Cover:
├─ (Age:18, Income:Low)
├─ (Age:18, Credit:Poor)
├─ (Income:Low, Employment:Self-Employed)
├─ (Credit:Poor, Assets:None)
└─ ... many more pairs

Optimized Test Cases: ~18 cases
(Instead of 270!)

These 18 cases cover ALL important pairs
```

**Pairwise Tool Example:**

```
Input:
Age: 18, 25, 35, 50, 65
Income: Low, Med, High
Credit: Poor, Fair, Good
Employment: Emp, Self, Ret
Assets: None, Some, Sub

Generated Pairwise Tests (optimized):
┌──────┬────────┬───────┬────────┬───────┐
│ Age  │ Income │ Credit│ Employ │Assets │
├──────┼────────┼───────┼────────┼───────┤
│ 18   │ Low    │ Poor  │ Emp    │ None  │
│ 25   │ Med    │ Fair  │ Self   │ Some  │
│ 35   │ High   │ Good  │ Ret    │ Sub   │
│ 50   │ Low    │ Good  │ Self   │ None  │
│ 65   │ Med    │ Poor  │ Ret    │ Some  │
└──────┴────────┴───────┴────────┴───────┘

Result: All pairs covered in just 5 test cases!
(Instead of 270 exhaustive combinations)
```

