#### Q16: What is Mutation Testing?

**Theory:**
Mutation testing **introduces small changes (mutations)** to code and verifies tests catch them. It measures test quality.

**Purpose:**

```
Question: How good are my tests?

Answer: Are they good enough to catch bugs
        if code changed slightly?

Mutation Testing checks this!
```

**Example:**

```
Original Code:
──────────────
if (age >= 18) {
    canVote = true;
}


Test Cases:
───────────
@Test void testCanVote() {
    assertTrue(age(20) canVote());
}

@Test void testCannotVote() {
    assertFalse(age(17) canVote());
}


Mutation 1: Change >= to >
──────────────────────────
if (age > 18) {          // MUTATED!
    canVote = true;
}

Test Results:
- age(20) canVote(): Still ✓ PASS
- age(17) canVote(): Still ✓ PASS
- age(18) canVote(): ✗ FAIL (caught mutation!)

Quality: Good - tests caught this mutation


Mutation 2: Change >= to <=
──────────────────────────
if (age <= 18) {         // MUTATED!
    canVote = true;
}

Test Results:
- age(20) canVote(): ✗ FAIL (caught!)
- age(17) canVote(): ✓ PASS
- age(18) canVote(): Still needs test

Quality: Good - tests caught this mutation


Mutation 3: Change true to false
────────────────────────────────
if (age >= 18) {
    canVote = false;     // MUTATED!
}

Test Results:
- age(20) canVote(): ✓ PASS (unchanged!)
- age(17) canVote(): ✓ PASS (unchanged!)
Neither test fails!

Quality: BAD - tests didn't catch mutation!

Recommendation: Need better test or add:
@Test void testAge18CanVote() {
    assertTrue(age(18) canVote());  // Catches this mutation
}
```

**Mutation Score:**

```
Mutation Testing Report:
────────────────────────
Total Mutations Created: 50
Mutations Killed (caught): 48
Mutations Survived (missed): 2

Mutation Score = 48/50 = 96%

Interpretation:
✓ High score (>80%) = Tests are good
✓ Medium score (60-80%) = Tests need improvement
✗ Low score (<60%) = Tests need work

If score is low:
- Add more test cases
- Test more edge cases
- Improve assertions
